WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.530
Revenge Trap
Out of Control!  Paracide

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.000
Jonouchi!

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.780
Hey, Yugi and Mai!

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:39.730
Hi!

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.220
You're still alive.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.150
Of course!  You should worry about yourself instead of me!

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.400
There's no need for that.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.700
You already gathered four?

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.300
You're awesome, Mai!

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.200
I have three, and Jonouchi has two.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.940
When we three get together, I'm always at the bottom.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.370
The other duelists had at least one duel since yesterday.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.250
That means half are eliminated.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.960
Eight duelists will make the finals, so we can't be wasting time.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.250
I know!

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.080
I'll go search for my prey.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.420
Don't you dare lose before the finals.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.640
Okay!

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.120
I'll see you at the finals!

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.600
Maybe I'll encounter today the God Card that Marik mentioned.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.510
What?  Yugi already left?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.180
Yeah.  He was in high spirits today.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.810
Sheesh!  It's because you were late, Honda!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.580
My phone call with Shizuka lasted longer than I expected.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.660
I wanted to hang up, but she wouldn't let me.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.000
Isn't it the other way around?

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.290
It'll be difficult to find him in the city.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.230
In that case, it'll be easier to find him if you have more people.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:06.820
To become a true duelist, I can't duel against weaklings.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.200
But I can't find anyone.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.400
Hey, mister.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.200
What's up?

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.740
Can I have your autograph?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.920
You're a Battle City duelist, right?

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.990
I see!  I must be pretty famous!

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.260
You want my autograph that badly?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.620
Yeah!  I'm getting autographs from every duelist I meet!

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.540
Because if one of them becomes the champion, it'll be worth a lot of money!

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.900
Well...  He's still my fan, after all.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.060
That Duel Disk is awesome!

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:43.370
Right?  It proves that I'm a specially ranked duelist.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:47.420
Mister, let me try it on for a little while!

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:47.850
What?

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.060
C'mon!  Please!

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.710
I guess I can't say "no" to a fan.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.370
Here you go.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.080
So cool!

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.300
Handle it with care.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.100
It represents a duelist's soul, so the only thing more important than my Duel Disk is my life!

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.680
Hey, punk!  Freeze!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.130
I wonder where he is.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:13.640
When searching on foot, you realize Domino City is a lot bigger than it seems.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.070
Maybe not.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.260
Jonouchi!

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.210
Why is he so angry?

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.140
Wait!

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.760
The Duel Disk?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:28.860
Hey!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.580
Let me go!

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.550
Honda!

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.990
What are you doing?

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.770
Why don't you ask him!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.280
I'm sorry.  I wanted to get revenge.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.360
Revenge?

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:48.370
I came to watch the duels, but over at that park...

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.280
What?

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.200
This guy took my rare cards, so I wanted to beat him a duel.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.200
That's no reason to steal someone else's Duel Disk.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.530
That makes you no different than the guy who took your cards.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.750
I'm sorry.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.290
Who took your cards?

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.510
Umm...  He had weird round glasses and a bowl haircut.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:15.680
Evil eyes and a weird laugh.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.680
Insector Haga!

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.830
He's still up to his old tricks!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.270
Unforgivable!

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.200
I've decided that Insector Haga will be my next opponent!

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.110
He's in the park, right?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:28.570
Yeah.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:29.600
Jonouchi!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.660
Wait up!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.640
Bye bye.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.030
Good luck, Mister!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.250
Did you do as I said?

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:44.920
Yes!

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.120
He was much easier to fool than I expected.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.580
Now I can definitely crush Jonouchi.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:54.620
His deck is...

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.570
Haga, you promised me a rare card!

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.010
Oh yeah.  Here you go.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.170
Thanks-  Huh?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.150
This is Gokibore!

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.660
It's not a rare card!

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.900
You don't deserve a rare card.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.020
What?

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.470
Take this instead!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.860
I'll defeat Jonouchi to bring Yugi to me.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.710
I'll pay him back in double for humiliating me at Duelist Kingdom!

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.500
Using my Super Insect Deck.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.050
Kenta!  Where are you?

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.540
Shizuka, did someone come in here?

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.800
What's going on?

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.300
A boy named Kenta doesn't want to leave the hospital, so he's running and hiding.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.280
He doesn't want to leave?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.930
I don't know why.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.660
He's such a troublemaker.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.330
It's safe to come out.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.600
You knew I was here?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.080
I can still sense when people are around.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.680
Why didn't you rat me out?

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.420
We should help each other when we're in trouble.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.680
Besides, I don't get along with that nurse.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.310
Then I want to help you too.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.350
What should I do?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.620
Hmm...

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:26.660
Can you tell me what's on the computer?

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:30.110
Is this the Battle City homepage?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.460
My brother is in the tournament.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:36.200
Dammit!  Where did Haga go?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.640
He's not here anymore?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.070
Long time no see, Jonouchi.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.800
There you are, Insector Haga!

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:47.640
I was looking forward to meeting you again.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:52.010
You threatened and stole a kid's rare cards!

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.420
Is that what he said?

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.460
I'll make sure you won't do that again.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:58.800
Wait, Honda.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.900
I challenge you to a duel.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.500
Wait a sec, Jonouchi!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.500
You don't have to duel him.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.600
He's a cheater who threw Yugi's cards into the ocean!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:15.440
Even though you hate me, I'm honored that a cute girl remembers me.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:22.650
Jonouchi, let's bet our Puzzle Card and two rare cards.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:23.740
Two?

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:27.770
That means if Jonouchi loses this duel, he's eliminated.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.590
Don't do it, Jonouchi!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.130
What?  Are you scared?

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.390
Fine!

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:34.520
Jonouchi!

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:42.280
He lost to Yugi in his first duel at Duelist Kingdom, but he was once the Japan champion.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.970
He's a worthy opponent.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.840
You fool.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.910
You don't know I messed with your deck.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.170
When duelists meet in this city...

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.750
...it turns into Battle City!

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:04.760
Duel!

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.190
I go first!

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.200
Swordsman of Landstar in attack position!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.450
And I set one card.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.100
I end my turn.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.680
What a wimpy monster.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.800
It can handle your bugs with no problem!

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.270
It's my turn.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.920
Come out, Flying Kamakiri #1!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.150
Destroy Jonouchi's monster!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.120
I activate my set card!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.120
Shield & Sword!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.940
It swaps attack and defense points!

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.960
Flying Kamakiri #1 is destroyed!

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.100
How's that!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.840
Whatever.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.430
When Flying Kamakiri #1 is sent to the graveyard...

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:56.870
...I can bring out a Wind Attribute monster with 1500 or fewer attack points.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:01.540
I may have lost a few life points, but you haven't defeated me yet.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.560
Umm...  Katsuya Jonouchi, right?

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:06.350
That's right.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.800
He's dueling the former Japan champion!

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:11.290
What?

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:13.930
He'll be fine.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:18.160
My brother finished second at Duelist Kingdom.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.200
Really?

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.100
That's weird...

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.730
It says he's a level 2 nobody.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:27.600
My turn!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:34.980
If I don't do something now, Swordsman of Landstar will be destroyed next turn.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.720
What's the matter?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.720
Are you already out of options?

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.120
Jonouchi...

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.000
Whatever!

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.990
I tribute Swordsman of Landstar.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:51.000
I summon Jinzo!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.730
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.540
2400 attack points?

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.500
Way to go, Jonouchi!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.970
Keep it up!

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:06.500
My turn.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.220
A monster in defense position.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.350
I end my turn.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.830
I'll stay on the offensive!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.790
Jinzo, destroy that card!

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.320
What?

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.360
I got you.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.940
Kiseitai latches on to the monster that attacked it.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:35.370
Every time it's your turn, half your monster's attack points are added to my life points.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.240
What?

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.170
That's gross.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:46.050
I'll show you how terrifying my Super Insect Deck is!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.100
I set a monster in defense position and end my turn.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:06.800
My turn.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.910
I gained 1200 life points.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.330
Damn!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.060
Jinzo, attack!

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.250
Thanks!

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.690
What?  He gained life points again?

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:32.130
When Skull-Mark Ladybug goes to the graveyard, I gain 500 life points.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.130
Now I have more life points than you.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:39.050
There are many tricky insect monsters.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.440
He's playing right into Insector Haga's hands.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.000
My turn.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.820
A monster in defense position.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.210
It's your turn.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.150
I gain life points!

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.120
Defense position again?

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.820
Whenever I attack, he activates a weird effect.

00:12:56.070 --> 00:13:00.750
But if I let my turns pass me by, Haga will keep gaining life points.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.400
Who's winning?

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:06.290
It looks like your brother is losing.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:07.440
I see...

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:11.470
Your brother is unlucky to be matched up against a strong duelist.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.130
I bet my brother knew his opponent was tough, but he challenged him anyways.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:17.760
Why?

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.170
That's his way.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.710
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.720
That's pointless.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.390
What's impossible is impossible.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:34.060
But my brother will still duel fair and square.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.500
Believing in his own power.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.130
My turn!

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.710
I summon Panther Warrior!

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:50.000
Panther Warrior can't attack unless I tribute a monster on my field.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:56.020
I'll use that to my advantage to tribute Jinzo and attack!

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.320
Hooray!  Haga can't gain life points anymore!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:08.320
Nice thinking, Jonouchi.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:15.500
You finally got rid of Kiseitai, but I regained more than enough life points.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:22.330
And you're happy that you destroyed Pinch Hopper, but its effect lets me summon a monster from my hand.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.370
I summon Larvae Moth.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:29.600
Dammit!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.280
He always has a monster on his field!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:39.250
No matter how many you insects you squish, my deck can bring out more!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.190
I equip Cocoon of Evolution on Larvae Moth.

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:48.740
That's...

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.040
That's right.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:58.400
I failed to summon its final form at Duelist Kingdom, but I'll succeed this time!

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:01.910
Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.840
He won't win.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.600
This ex-champ is very tough.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:10.360
His cards are much stronger than your brother's.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.520
But my brother hasn't lost yet.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:16.140
You really don't know anything about cards.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.960
He can't win!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.330
Jonouchi.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:26.770
Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth will be born in five turns.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.420
I have to destroy that Cocoon!

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.300
Too bad, Jonouchi.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:34.730
You can't stop Cocoon of Evolution.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:38.010
You lost before this duel even started.

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:38.880
What?

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.820
Take this!  The spell card Reckless Parasite!

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.900
This card will drive your deck's Parasite Paracide crazy.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.970
What are you talking about?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.140
My deck doesn't have insect cards.

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:54.760
What?

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:05.740
Paracide implants a parasite in every monster you summon and transforms them into insects.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:07.770
What is that?

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.770
Jonouchi, why are you using a card that helps your opponent?

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:15.180
Like I said, I never put this card in my deck-

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.020
Can it be?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.420
You used that kid!

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:23.890
A great strategist prepares before the start of battle.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.590
That's cheating!

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.250
You're dirty!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.600
Oh really?

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:34.510
Can you call yourself a duelist if you don't check your deck before the start of a duel?

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:35.680
You...

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:41.060
Insect monsters will fill up both of our fields.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:45.950
I set a card and end my turn.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.620
I'll make you pay for tricking me!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.290
My monsters may be insects, but they still have the same attack and defense points.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:59.070
Oh, I forgot to mention that you can't tribute monsters that are infected with a parasite.

00:16:59.070 --> 00:16:59.760
What?

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:03.430
You can no longer summon high Level monsters.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:08.400
And Panther Warrior can't attack without tributing, so it's useless.

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.240
I summon Little-Winguard!

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.550
It's smart to strengthen your defenses.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:25.300
Actually, Little-Winguard attacks Cocoon of Evolution!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.720
Your monster is too weak against Cocoon's 2000 defense points.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:31.220
Look at your field more carefully!

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:33.740
Oh no!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.960
Cocoon of Evolution is in attack position!

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:37.420
That's right.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:41.680
Little-Winguard, attack Cocoon of Evolution!

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:44.370
Don't do it!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.410
Just kidding.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.710
I flip over my Continuous Spell Insect Barrier!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:18:01.280
I told you that all your monsters are now parasitic insect monsters.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:05.290
So as long as I have this card, your attacks can't reach me.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:06.990
What?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:11.700
That means Jonouchi can't summon high Level monsters nor attack!

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.320
Jonouchi's deck is completely locked down.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.960
That boy has scary strategies.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:25.610
Jonouchi, four more turns until Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth emerges from its cocoon.

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:29.570
Wow.  He's really going to summon Great Moth.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.570
Is Great Moth strong?

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:36.490
There aren't many monsters stronger than it.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:37.880
I see...

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.130
It's over for him.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.310
But...

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:45.360
Even if you believe in yourself, you can't win against someone who's stronger.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.730
Big brother...

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:52.740
I don't feel like waiting until Cocoon of Evolution opens up.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:58.510
I'll get rid of some of your life points so that Great Moth can defeat you with one strike.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:04.480
Good!  He has to destroy all my monsters if he wants to damage my life points.

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.160
If Parasite Paracide is gone, I can turn the tables.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.090
Leghul in attack position!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.900
It attacks you directly!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.880
A direct attack?

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.700
Leghul can attack you directly.

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:30.360
Did you expect me to do you a favor by getting rid of Parasite Paracide?

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:35.810
I switch all my monsters to defense position and end my turn.

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.410
That's pointless.

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:40.120
Continue the countdown to your death!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.750
Three turns until I summon Great Moth.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:44.400
But before that...

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.750
Leghul, attack him directly!

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.200
Two turns left.

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.250
Leghul, attack him directly!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:03.880
If you beg, I'm willing to reconsider my decision to summon Great Moth.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.810
Stop talking, you cheater!

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.400
Stop, Honda.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.750
Yugi taught me in the previous duel.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:23.000
Even if the opponent cheats, a true duelist fights fair and square... and wins!

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:29.440
Yugi, I'll become a true duelist during Battle City!

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.640
My monster in defense position!

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:39.610
I set one card and end my turn.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.080
Turn Alligator's Sword into a parasite!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.490
You're always on the defense.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.060
So what?

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:51.490
I'll keep going until I run out of life points!

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:53.430
I haven't lost yet!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.930
You don't know when to give up.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:21:00.370
I'll show you that you have no chance to win.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.040
It's my turn.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.340
Come out, Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth!

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.110
Show us your beauty!

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.920
So that's Perfectly Ultimate...

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:21.590
...Great Moth!

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:42.370
Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth finally emerged.

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:47.130
But Parasite Paracide still has sealed away Jonouchi's high Level monsters.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:49.000
How is he supposed to fight back?

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:52.160
A Dice card?  That's the ticket!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:55.330
Great Moth is destroyed, but that joy lasts only for a moment.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:58.300
He has a more powerful monster - Insect Queen!

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.100
Don't give up, Jonouchi!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:02.230
Fulfill your promise with Yugi!

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:05.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Gearfried the Iron Knight

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:06.800
Duel, standby!

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:25.430
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.230 --> 00:22:30.800
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:40.480
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:51.990
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:59.500
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:04.770
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:09.880
Will never change

00:23:10.540 --> 00:23:15.150
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:20.350
To be who I am

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:25.590
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:30.300
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.230
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:40.340
From now until forever...
